# Build outputs (redirected to a build sibling out of the source tree; ignored in-tree as a safety net)
bin/
obj/
dist/
build/
node_modules/
**/prefab/
src/runspace/boringssl/

# Binary artifacts — including the root-delivered full-fat builds (subsystem-win.exe, subsystem.apk)
*.apk
*.aar
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.exe
# Prebuilt native libraries are build outputs — rebuilt from source (e.g. src/native/directport/build.ps1).
*.dll
# ONNX model weights are re-derivable data (public Kokoro-82M etc.), NEVER in the repo — guard the
# vendored dpx engine (src/native/dpx) from ever swallowing a ~310 MB model.onnx.
*.onnx
# Compiled shader blobs — re-derivable from the .hlsl source (dxc/D3DCompile).
*.dxil
*.cso
# rename-aside debris from `ss build` self-replace
*.exe.old
# the embedded source payload — regenerated on every build, free to recreate
ss-source.dump

# EXCEPTION (#53): the VirtuaCam native artifacts are BUNDLED deliberately. They are an external
# toolchain's stable output (WDK/WIL/CMake) — treated like an OS DLL, NOT rebuilt in ss's pipeline —
# so the bundle must ship with the repo (clone-reproducible). Negate *.dll/*.exe for this one dir.
!src/native/virtuacam/*.dll
!src/native/virtuacam/*.exe

# Local-only siblings at the repo ROOT — NOT in the repo (kept as <drive>\ siblings).
# Root-anchored (leading /) so they NEVER collaterally ignore an in-tree dir of the same
# name — e.g. src/runspace/scripts/zoo (the .ps1 cmdlet zoo) must stay tracked + shippable.
/examples/
/models/
/reference/
/scratch/
/scripts/
/temp-build/
/workorders/
/notifications/

# Private working docs — the public repo ships the finished artifact, not the workshop.
# Rewritten docs return here one at a time as they are published.
/docs/
/CLAUDE.md
# Session scratch: handoffs, prompts, the parallel agent-session log, and the hle import staging
# (folded into canonical files like ss-log.md when published). Root-anchored so AGENTWEBVIEW-HANDOFF.md
# (already tracked) is unaffected.
/AGENT-HANDOFF.md
/HANDOFF-*.md
/PROMPT-*.md
/SSRD-HANDOFF.md
/ss-log-agent.md
/hle-import/

# Debug captures (safety net if new ones land at root)
/disp-*.png
/screen-*.png
/src/bugreport.txt

# Env / IDE
.env
.idea/
.vs/
.claude/
*.user
*.suo

# Backups
*robocopy*
*backup*

# SQLite Database Files
*.db

# === md gate: ss IS the docs; markdown is opt-in, never a handoff/side-store ===
*.md
!README.md
!Registry/Feedback/in-memoriam-dedication.md
# the vendored dpx engine carries its own provenance README (CRQ143 P0)
!src/native/dpx/README.md
# wip/ is the workshop: parked scattered projects (clone-and-rebuild sovereignty).
# Their docs/state ARE the point, so md is tracked under wip (heavy data still ignored
# by the *.dll/*.exe/*.onnx/*.zip/bin/obj rules above).
!wip/**/*.md
!wip/**/README.md
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
**/scratch/
**/.system_generated/

# self-build backups — local only, never pushed (GitHub 100MB wall)
ss.exe.*.old
ss.exe.old*
ss.exe.prev
tmpss-*.exe
src/native/qnnworker/mm_qnn
